# Valkyrie

A desktop application template: Wails v3, an embedded PocketBase, a React frontend. The domain belongs to the application; the
scaffolding is shared.

The canonical guides are `AGENTS.md` (working rules, commands, change routing), `CONTEXT.md` (vocabulary),
`docs/architecture.md` (why), and `docs/troubleshooting.md` (what breaks). Read `AGENTS.md` before making a change.

## The one concept

**The job queue is generic; the runner is yours.**

`internal/jobs` owns the lifecycle only: persistence, bounded concurrency, cancellation, status transitions, the Wails event
push. A job is a title, a prompt, a `map[string]any` of params and an arbitrary result. The work goes to a `jobs.Runner`.

The application replaces `internal/runner/echo.go` and changes nothing else. **Never put domain logic in `internal/jobs/`.**

## Rules

- The frontend never talks to PocketBase or a remote API directly. Go through `internal/bindings/service.go` and the wrappers
  in `frontend/src/bindings/index.ts`.
- Never hand-edit `frontend/bindings/` or `frontend/dist/`. Both are generated and gitignored.
- Never edit an applied migration. A new migration needs a later timestamp in the file name and must be idempotent.
- `app_settings` has no access rule. That is what keeps the secrets away from the HTTP API. Never add one.
- Sizes in the stylesheet are in `rem`; the zoom scales the root font size.
- The generated bindings type a missing array as nullable. Normalise it in the wrapper, not in the components.

## Commands

`wails3` lives in `~/go/bin` and is not on the default PATH of a non-interactive shell.

```bash
PATH="$HOME/go/bin:$PATH" wails3 build
PATH="$HOME/go/bin:$PATH" wails3 task common:generate:bindings
go test -race ./internal/... .
cd frontend && npm run typecheck && npm test
python3 tools/license-audit.py
```

`go build ./...` fails on `build/ios` by design. Build `./internal/... .` instead.

## Before finishing

Run the checks that match what you changed. The routing table is in `AGENTS.md`. When in doubt:

```bash
gofmt -l internal/ main.go main_test.go tools/
go vet ./internal/... .
go test -race ./internal/... .
cd frontend && npm run typecheck && npm test && npm run build && cd ..
python3 tools/license-audit.py
```
